commit a9840ccb80c4a9dfb6b692650d32c1ae847e25d1
Author: authorss81 <authorss81@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 5 17:13:58 2026 +0530

    Fix a bare `catch` being silently deleted by the VM and the formatter
    
    `catch` with no name binding is legal: the parser leaves `catch_var` as `None`
    and still collects the body. Both consumers tested the Option instead of
    checking whether a catch was present, so a bare catch was treated as no catch
    at all:
    
      vm.rs        the handler never ran, and control then fell through to
                   `Ok(Value::Nothing)` — the error was swallowed and the program
                   carried on as if nothing had failed. The interpreter was
                   reporting success for a run that had faulted.
      formatter.rs the whole `catch` block was omitted, so formatting DELETED the
                   statements the user wrote.
    
    Found by the reviewer on phase-015, which it flagged three rounds running. The
    third-round finding is the one that mattered and it is the reason the fix pass
    existed: the pass reported the fix in its summary table while the `if let
    Some(var)` arm was untouched, so the reviewer correctly refused to approve.
    
    Both sites now ask whether a catch is present — `catch_var.is_some() ||
    !catch_body.is_empty()` — and the VM propagates the error when there is no
    handler instead of discarding it. The named form is unchanged.
    
    Tests, with red-before-green:
    
      edge_bare_catch_program_still_computes_the_same_after_formatting FAILS with
